WEBVTT

00:00.430 --> 00:04.940
<b>Two weeks before the Decay of Angels incident...</b>

00:15.090 --> 00:16.230
Heya.

00:16.230 --> 00:17.160
Dazai-san.

00:17.590 --> 00:20.030
Sorry for dragging you out 
here out of the blue,

00:20.030 --> 00:23.180
but we won't have to worry 
about surveillance here.

00:23.610 --> 00:27.190
We're the only ones who 
know about this place.

00:27.190 --> 00:28.080
Indeed.

00:28.890 --> 00:31.060
This is where you and I...

00:31.860 --> 00:33.430
I need to ask for a favor.

00:34.780 --> 00:36.950
The world is about to be torn,

00:36.950 --> 00:41.520
and from the fissure a deep, 
dark state of chaos will emerge.

00:42.290 --> 00:45.750
When that happens,
I'd like you to be my eyes.

00:45.750 --> 00:46.810
Your eyes?

00:46.810 --> 00:49.140
Eyes to watch over all things.

00:49.140 --> 00:54.820
Never siding with anyone, never 
interfering, and hence never detected.

00:54.820 --> 00:56.120
That's you.

00:56.760 --> 01:00.810
I need your help to save this world, 
the Detective Agency, and Atsushi-kun.

01:01.020 --> 01:02.040
I refuse!

01:02.610 --> 01:07.210
Whatever colors the flames that engulf
the world or the Agency are, I don't care.

01:07.210 --> 01:10.250
Much less would I ever save the weretiger.

01:10.250 --> 01:11.290
Sure you will.

01:13.060 --> 01:16.080
You know why, don't you?

01:20.040 --> 01:22.560
A flash of the sword creates pain.

01:22.560 --> 01:25.230
And a flash can end it.

01:25.750 --> 01:27.380
I'll put you at ease.

01:27.380 --> 01:30.060
You won't need to do that.

01:31.040 --> 01:34.370
For every time that weretiger 
is plunged into suffering,

01:34.370 --> 01:37.250
he returns as an even 
more troublesome enemy.

01:37.520 --> 01:39.730
Akutagawa! Why are you here?

01:40.100 --> 01:41.970
By Dazai-san's orders.

01:43.410 --> 01:46.570
To collect information,
detected by neither friend nor foe.

01:46.830 --> 01:50.050
To never aid unless a 
smoke signal is seen.

01:50.580 --> 01:51.880
Those were his orders.

01:51.880 --> 01:54.070
Rampo-san's smoke flare!

01:54.820 --> 01:57.110
Rampo-san predicted that, too?

01:58.260 --> 01:59.500
Another one!

01:59.830 --> 02:04.110
And this one looks like a 
pain in the ass to shut up.

02:04.110 --> 02:07.040
I have no intention of revealing 
your identity to the outside.

02:07.040 --> 02:08.490
Is that so?

02:08.490 --> 02:11.260
My job is to feed the fish.

02:11.530 --> 02:13.860
I'll be sending you into the ocean minced.

02:13.860 --> 02:17.240
The meat of a mastermind ought 
to be quite nourishing.

02:22.280 --> 02:24.900
What an insolent Gifted you are!

02:24.900 --> 02:26.490
Can't you see that I'm your senior!

02:26.490 --> 02:28.920
All lives are equal.

02:28.920 --> 02:31.000
Why are you always this way?

02:31.370 --> 02:35.490
You should be escaping to report the truth!

02:35.490 --> 02:38.340
You're the one who's oblivious 
to the situation, weretiger.

02:38.730 --> 02:41.040
How can you not notice this opportunity?

02:44.670 --> 02:45.930
What was that?

02:45.930 --> 02:49.300
I destroyed the engine room 
to trap the ship here.

02:49.710 --> 02:51.940
No one can send backup now.

02:52.720 --> 02:53.650
In other words...

02:54.240 --> 02:57.240
For just this moment, he's all by himself.

02:58.620 --> 03:02.530
<i>The moment I knew this man was my enemy, 
I became fearful of loneliness.</i>

03:03.140 --> 03:06.070
<i>But he's the one who's alone right now.</i>

03:06.070 --> 03:08.580
We'll slash his throat and close the case.

03:09.880 --> 03:11.160
Just the two of us?

03:11.490 --> 03:13.410
Do we need any more?

03:14.140 --> 03:15.930
Why me?

03:16.910 --> 03:21.600
You've got plenty of people to work for you 
who are stronger and more intelligent than I am.

03:22.410 --> 03:24.880
Do you remember when we first met?

03:25.230 --> 03:30.440
I'd remember that night, even if I'd 
forgotten every other detail of my life.

03:33.480 --> 03:36.350
Can you give me a reason to live?

03:36.970 --> 03:38.570
I can.

03:39.180 --> 03:42.640
Why did I invite you into 
the Mafia that day?

03:43.100 --> 03:45.790
Why did I make you work 
alongside Atsushi-kun?

03:46.400 --> 03:48.120
To develop a special weapon 
against the Demon.

03:48.520 --> 03:53.000
To make a new generation of Double Black.

03:53.640 --> 03:54.490
In other words...

03:55.340 --> 03:57.220
<i>For this moment.</i>

03:57.220 --> 03:58.220
Now, then...

03:58.660 --> 04:04.420
Whatever path you choose, 
I will congratulate you.

04:04.870 --> 04:08.760
Young men, choose a path that 
won't leave your souls to regret.

04:08.760 --> 04:11.880
Especially if you will perish anyway!

04:12.120 --> 04:13.500
I need thirty seconds.

04:13.500 --> 04:14.520
Fix your leg.

04:15.600 --> 04:18.690
<b><i>Tenma Tengai</i></b>

04:16.380 --> 04:17.430
Tenma Tengai!

04:19.500 --> 04:21.080
It's a mere metal rod!

04:21.080 --> 04:22.200
Avoid it, Akutagawa!

04:31.060 --> 04:32.010
What the...

04:32.400 --> 04:33.410
Did something hit us?

04:33.650 --> 04:35.510
It's not just the weapon.

04:35.880 --> 04:37.340
It doesn't matter if it's just railing...

04:37.340 --> 04:40.220
He makes it into a weapon a 
thousand times more powerful.

04:40.650 --> 04:42.590
You dodged it.

04:42.590 --> 04:45.670
I should be careful not to sink 
the ship with my next swing.

04:46.150 --> 04:47.440
You freak.

04:50.100 --> 04:51.030
<i>Too fast!</i>

04:51.360 --> 04:52.670
<i>I can't avoid it!</i>

04:53.660 --> 04:54.590
<i>But...</i>

04:55.010 --> 04:58.770
<i>Dazai-san didn't abandoned me.</i>

04:58.770 --> 05:00.450
<i>Everything is a trial.</i>

05:00.730 --> 05:03.150
<i>And so I'll overcome death itself!</i>

05:04.030 --> 05:06.950
<b><b>Rashoumon</b></b>

05:05.340 --> 05:08.990
Rashoumon: Tenma Agito!

05:25.880 --> 05:27.290
<i>I don't stand a chance in this position.</i>

05:29.650 --> 05:30.670
Weretiger!

05:37.930 --> 05:39.040
Don't touch me!

05:39.040 --> 05:40.100
You disgust me!

05:40.670 --> 05:42.180
Why did you run?

05:42.480 --> 05:44.270
The mission is to destroy him!

05:44.270 --> 05:45.330
There's no way!

05:45.330 --> 05:46.400
You saw him!

05:46.400 --> 05:49.400
He's a god of war in human form!

05:49.400 --> 05:52.490
I'll defeat him even if it means seeing 
every bone in my body crumble.

05:52.780 --> 05:53.780
Why?!

05:54.490 --> 05:58.050
Because otherwise Dazai
won't need me anymore.

05:59.370 --> 06:02.790
Four years ago, Dazai-san abandoned me,

06:03.190 --> 06:06.280
and replaced me with the 
shiny new thing that was you.

06:06.770 --> 06:07.590
But...

06:09.630 --> 06:11.430
Perhaps I'm wrong.

06:11.870 --> 06:13.950
Isn't everything a trial?

06:14.530 --> 06:19.190
Is it not all an extension of the purpose 
given to me in that forest that night?

06:19.440 --> 06:20.780
A trial?

06:20.780 --> 06:22.500
Fukuchi Ouchi is?

06:22.500 --> 06:23.520
No.

06:24.340 --> 06:25.700
You are.

06:26.370 --> 06:28.160
Ah, shit, I overslept.

06:28.680 --> 06:31.050
I can't believe it took the 
intruder alert to wake us up.

06:33.580 --> 06:34.310
Wait!

06:34.310 --> 06:34.940
I surrender!

06:36.030 --> 06:39.500
I don't get paid enough 
to die with a villain!

06:40.670 --> 06:44.510
I mean, believe it or not,
I have an adorable wife and daughter.

06:44.510 --> 06:50.550
Basically, if I were to let a terrorist get away
 and go on to destroy my home, I'd be upset.

07:02.750 --> 07:04.120
Stop, Akutagawa!

07:04.120 --> 07:04.700
Don't kill him!

07:04.980 --> 07:06.490
Shut up.

07:12.940 --> 07:13.900
Shit!

07:18.110 --> 07:19.170
He's alive.

07:19.790 --> 07:21.450
That was his carotid artery.

07:21.950 --> 07:25.970
Squeezing it causes fainting due 
to lack of blood to the brain.

07:25.970 --> 07:27.720
He'll regain consciousness in a few minutes.

07:28.150 --> 07:29.460
So you...

07:29.880 --> 07:32.680
You haven't killed anyone 
since we made that promise?

07:32.970 --> 07:36.140
Don't kill anyone for the next six months.

07:36.140 --> 07:38.610
I keep my promises.

07:39.570 --> 07:40.960
Are you sure you heard gunshots?

07:41.400 --> 07:42.930
Yeah, this way.

07:44.770 --> 07:45.720
Damn.

07:45.720 --> 07:46.850
Let's go.

07:47.500 --> 07:50.360
That said, we need to think of something.

07:51.120 --> 07:52.730
The answer is simple.

07:52.730 --> 07:54.070
We defeat Fukuchi.

07:54.550 --> 07:57.660
If only it were that easy!

07:57.660 --> 07:58.930
There is a way.

07:59.610 --> 08:01.320
Of course there is.

08:01.320 --> 08:04.930
Dazai-san would never have made us work 
together without a strategy in mind.

08:09.400 --> 08:12.790
There's a simple, yet absolute, tactic.

08:14.130 --> 08:17.580
Beast Beneath the Moonlight Rashoumon, 
Kokko Zessou.

08:18.290 --> 08:21.100
This is the one we used in 
the fight against Fyodor.

08:21.340 --> 08:24.100
An amalgam of our special abilities.

08:24.100 --> 08:27.850
Those claws can even kill a god,
if you can hit them.

08:28.790 --> 08:30.580
There's just one problem.

08:31.090 --> 08:32.070
I'm sure you know.

08:32.540 --> 08:33.310
Yeah.

08:33.650 --> 08:35.320
Actually hitting them.

08:35.670 --> 08:39.050
Our enemy is particularly evasive.

08:39.370 --> 08:42.290
Thus, there will not be a second chance 
to use Kokko Zessou.

08:42.610 --> 08:45.750
The entirety of my power
 will be passed to you.

08:45.750 --> 08:50.590
Should we be outed,
my head will be the first to fly.

08:50.890 --> 08:53.340
End him on the first strike.

08:53.340 --> 08:55.310
Then we'll have to go underwater.

08:55.720 --> 08:58.980
We won't be as nimble in the water,

08:58.980 --> 09:02.600
but Kokko Zessou has a longer range.

09:03.060 --> 09:04.790
And there's just the thing here for it.

09:04.790 --> 09:05.750
This way.

09:07.170 --> 09:11.600
There's a submarine for rescuing government 
VIPs in the event of an emergency.

09:11.600 --> 09:13.520
We can launch it unmanned.

09:13.520 --> 09:15.450
He'll have no choice but to go after it,

09:16.620 --> 09:18.730
and that's when we'll ambush him from behind.

09:19.310 --> 09:20.400
<i>Please...</i>

09:20.400 --> 09:21.770
<i>I hope this works.</i>

09:36.050 --> 09:39.050
<b>Episode 53</b>

09:36.530 --> 09:37.880
We've failed.

09:44.770 --> 09:46.680
You don't need to look so furious.

09:47.010 --> 09:48.680
<i>Was he on to us?</i>

09:49.270 --> 09:51.800
I'm not going to torment you or anything.

09:53.130 --> 09:54.950
Why do you do this?

09:55.310 --> 09:57.980
Is it because the battlefield changed you?

09:57.980 --> 10:00.560
Were you tortured by the enemy or something?

10:01.020 --> 10:04.570
Yeah, I've certainly experienced torture.

10:05.240 --> 10:07.780
Though I was on the torturing side.

10:08.900 --> 10:10.500
Not just soldiers.

10:11.030 --> 10:13.210
Civilians, too.

10:13.210 --> 10:15.260
Women and children.

10:15.920 --> 10:19.180
<b>On that battlefield,
I was born.</b>

10:19.490 --> 10:23.210
Neither you nor Fukuzawa 
know that battlefield.

10:23.210 --> 10:26.840
That's why you can believe 
in a benevolent state.

10:28.190 --> 10:30.340
I challenge the justness of 
the heavens' directives!

10:30.340 --> 10:35.210
I've endured countless trials and tribulations, 
suffered hardships inconceivable in number,

10:35.210 --> 10:39.350
the lack of recognition of which fuels my wrath.

10:39.580 --> 10:45.860
Thus I, humble Ouchi, shall embrace
 the cold cynicism of all creation!

10:46.550 --> 10:48.680
Come fight, young whelps!

10:57.460 --> 10:59.430
<b><i>Tenma Agito</i></b>

10:57.860 --> 10:59.420
Tenma Agito!

11:04.740 --> 11:05.400
What?!

11:20.730 --> 11:22.820
And stay down.

11:23.920 --> 11:26.430
Did you think you could defeat 
me if you fought together?

11:27.050 --> 11:31.650
I've defeated a hundred 
Gifted single-handedly.

11:32.210 --> 11:37.390
Should the two of you attack individually, 
I need only kill you individually.

11:37.390 --> 11:38.920
Stay down, you say?

11:39.570 --> 11:40.850
I refuse.

11:45.910 --> 11:48.690
He's using his ability and his coat
to force his bones into place.

11:49.590 --> 11:52.610
<i>I have to keep up with him.</i>

11:54.640 --> 11:55.870
Very well.

12:02.100 --> 12:05.430
I shall demonstrate the true 
nature of the battlefield.

12:07.910 --> 12:11.780
The battlefield is a garden of 
carnage whereupon justice,

12:11.780 --> 12:14.370
courage, and conviction die all the same.

12:14.370 --> 12:18.300
The only possible paths are a death 
that is merciful or one that is not.

12:20.290 --> 12:22.450
Welcome to the battlefield.

12:28.690 --> 12:34.580
This katana was forged by Gifted 
blacksmiths 1,500 years ago.

12:34.580 --> 12:36.470
It's noble, but peculiar.

12:36.830 --> 12:42.260
It had never been used in battle, as it was 
made specifically for ritual activities.

12:42.260 --> 12:44.440
Not until I wielded it.

12:44.440 --> 12:50.200
Let me tell you why you've lost:

12:51.100 --> 12:53.800
you shouldn't have made me draw this sword.

13:00.750 --> 13:01.930
Akutagawa!

13:02.740 --> 13:04.290
One down.

13:04.290 --> 13:07.020
<i>I didn't even see him move!</i>

13:07.270 --> 13:08.760
<i>What happened to him?</i>

13:08.760 --> 13:10.030
<i>He's coming.</i>

13:10.030 --> 13:11.630
<i>Something's coming.</i>

13:11.630 --> 13:14.260
<i>Something I have to evade.</i>

13:14.770 --> 13:15.740
<i>No...</i>

13:15.740 --> 13:18.390
<i>I can use the tiger's eyes 
to see what's coming.</i>

13:24.650 --> 13:26.830
The ritual sword Amenogozen.

13:26.830 --> 13:28.980
Otherwise known as the "space-time sword."

13:29.400 --> 13:33.200
It compresses space to 
send its blade elsewhere,

13:33.450 --> 13:37.420
but it could only traverse 
a dozen or so centimeters.

13:37.420 --> 13:41.570
Until it's been made a hundred times 
more powerful by my special ability!

13:46.020 --> 13:47.010
It's over.

13:47.010 --> 13:50.690
The tiger's abilities are 
effective in frontal attacks.

13:50.690 --> 13:54.190
The black coat abilities are effective 
in defense and attacking blind spots.

13:54.450 --> 13:59.650
With the tiger in front and the 
black coat in defense and ambush,

14:00.130 --> 14:03.310
you may have had my head.

14:04.040 --> 14:09.780
The only reason you failed, 
boy, is because you faltered.

14:10.230 --> 14:12.360
That's why I said...

14:12.750 --> 14:16.880
Should the two of you attack individually, 
I need only kill you individually.

14:18.580 --> 14:20.030
<i>He's right.</i>

14:20.480 --> 14:23.780
<i>But for that, I would have 
needed to trust Akutagawa</i>

14:23.780 --> 14:27.190
<i>and thrown myself into this 
freak's radius of murder.</i>

14:27.600 --> 14:30.400
<i>I could never have done 
such a reckless thing.</i>

14:33.040 --> 14:34.520
What's so funny?

14:35.070 --> 14:37.300
Because I'm happy, of course.

14:37.900 --> 14:40.600
Undefeated hero, Fukuchi Ouchi...

14:40.600 --> 14:45.570
If I defeat you,
Dazai-san will surely approve of me.

14:48.820 --> 14:51.580
Looks like you don't understand 
your own situation.

14:51.580 --> 14:53.400
You won't be surviving.

14:53.400 --> 14:56.060
You two won't even be given a swift death.

14:56.060 --> 15:00.090
I still need you to give me all the 
information you have, after all.

15:02.300 --> 15:05.700
Though, I'm a little tired 
of that kind of thing.

15:06.190 --> 15:08.690
Akutagawa-kun, was it?

15:08.690 --> 15:10.630
Why don't you become my apprentice?

15:11.110 --> 15:12.570
What?

15:12.570 --> 15:16.690
I'm more powerful and more 
experienced than anyone.

15:17.170 --> 15:21.960
More than anything, I'll soak my hands
in blood to achieve my goals. Like you.

15:21.960 --> 15:24.780
Is that not more appealing than 
the death you're suffering now?

15:25.350 --> 15:28.740
That's the most foolish 
proposition in the world.

15:29.140 --> 15:32.810
No one would replace Dazai-san!

15:33.250 --> 15:35.770
I never said to turn on him.

15:35.770 --> 15:39.780
My occupation has made me quite 
adept at training Gifted.

15:40.110 --> 15:43.680
Once you've become the strongest Gifted 
among even the Hunting Dogs,

15:43.680 --> 15:45.630
I'll return you to your master.

15:45.940 --> 15:48.630
There's no guarantee that 
you'll keep your promise!

15:49.450 --> 15:51.230
I'll uphold my promise.

15:52.080 --> 15:56.840
Besides, I have a reason 
to negotiate with you.

15:57.220 --> 15:59.500
I'd like you to do something for me.

16:00.360 --> 16:02.640
Kill the tiger boy.

16:04.060 --> 16:08.280
I've had enough of dispatching 
children for my objectives.

16:08.520 --> 16:12.460
You were never motivated by the just act 
of stopping a terrorist in the first place.

16:13.600 --> 16:16.420
In other words, you have 
no motivation to kill me.

16:16.740 --> 16:20.710
So shouldn't you make survival 
your priority for now?

16:22.120 --> 16:23.220
What's wrong?

16:23.220 --> 16:24.870
Don't you want to kill him?

16:24.870 --> 16:27.470
Is his life that important to you?

16:29.410 --> 16:31.110
Get up, weretiger.

16:31.110 --> 16:32.600
Good.

16:32.600 --> 16:33.790
No!

16:33.790 --> 16:36.270
Do you really think he'll keep his promise?

16:36.820 --> 16:40.390
I promised I would kill 
you in six months' time.

16:40.390 --> 16:42.420
That time's simply come a little sooner.

16:42.640 --> 16:44.460
I'll defeat you.

16:44.460 --> 16:46.360
That's my purpose in life.

16:46.630 --> 16:48.820
Why are you so obsessed with 
your purpose in life?!

16:50.490 --> 16:52.290
I haven't told anyone this...

16:52.290 --> 16:54.210
But I have an illness of the lung.

16:55.220 --> 16:56.820
My time is short.

16:57.170 --> 17:02.080
Therefore, I cannot allow myself to 
disappoint Dazai-san in the time I have left.

17:03.310 --> 17:04.790
I see.

17:06.390 --> 17:07.790
I'm sorry.

17:16.660 --> 17:21.490
<i>Akutagawa said he can't allow 
himself to disappoint Dazai-san.</i>

17:21.790 --> 17:26.760
<i>Then, if Akutagawa meets 
Dazai-san after I die...</i>

17:26.760 --> 17:30.810
<i>If Dazai-san learns that he betrayed 
me in order to survive...</i>

17:30.810 --> 17:32.770
<i>How would Dazai-san react?</i>

17:43.100 --> 17:43.870
What?!

17:44.640 --> 17:46.290
<i>A perfect ambush.</i>

17:46.710 --> 17:47.840
<i>This is trust!</i>

17:49.230 --> 17:51.070
Beast Beneath the Moonlight Rashoumon,

17:49.400 --> 17:50.060
<b><i>Beast Beneath the Moonlight</i></b>

17:50.060 --> 17:51.290
<b><i>Rashoumon</i></b>

17:51.300 --> 17:52.170
<b><i>Beast Beneath the Moonlight Rashoumon</i></b>

17:52.450 --> 17:54.120
Kokko Zessou!

18:11.560 --> 18:12.930
Don't die yet!

18:13.270 --> 18:16.370
Reveal the truth and the Detective 
Agency's innocence to the public!

18:16.900 --> 18:23.040
It seems Heaven still will not 
 release me from my duties...

18:27.220 --> 18:28.470
He's dead.

18:31.180 --> 18:32.450
Found it.

18:32.450 --> 18:33.570
The page!

18:33.570 --> 18:35.950
The Agency's saved.

18:35.950 --> 18:38.240
Then my mission is complete.

18:38.240 --> 18:40.350
We're getting out before security arrives.

18:42.240 --> 18:43.110
What's the matter?

18:46.400 --> 18:50.740
<i>What did that katana cut in the last moment?</i>

18:52.100 --> 18:53.390
What's the matter?

18:53.390 --> 18:55.360
<i>It never cut us.</i>

18:56.180 --> 18:59.610
<i>Where did that sword strike, in the end?</i>

19:21.210 --> 19:22.860
<i>A perfect ambush.</i>

19:23.250 --> 19:24.460
<i>This is trust!</i>

19:25.940 --> 19:27.940
Beast Beneath the Moonlight Rashoumon,

19:27.930 --> 19:28.810
<b><i>Beast Beneath the Moonlight Rashoumon</i></b>

19:29.100 --> 19:30.770
Kokko Zessou!

19:35.130 --> 19:36.180
Weretiger!

19:51.670 --> 19:52.690
What...

19:53.500 --> 19:55.000
What happened to me?

19:57.400 --> 19:59.640
That was a perfect ambush.

20:00.490 --> 20:03.100
He didn't even have time to defend himself.

20:03.650 --> 20:07.000
Anything you'd like to say before you die?

20:07.830 --> 20:09.100
What have you done?

20:09.450 --> 20:13.420
How do you think I've been able to save 
the world from disaster so many times?

20:13.420 --> 20:15.710
How do you think I've been 
victorious so many times?

20:16.370 --> 20:17.710
Didn't I tell you?

20:17.710 --> 20:20.120
Amenogozen is the space-time sword.

20:20.670 --> 20:23.210
Its blade traverses space.

20:23.210 --> 20:26.510
It also traverses time.

20:28.480 --> 20:31.670
You defeated me in the future, yes?

20:32.360 --> 20:36.660
But at the moment of my defeat, 
Amenogozen cut through to the past.

20:36.910 --> 20:40.270
As a result, your victory was rendered moot.

20:40.270 --> 20:41.180
It was erased.

20:41.730 --> 20:47.620
From the future, the blade cut the past,
so I never lost in the first place.

20:48.020 --> 20:49.710
<i>He's insurmountable.</i>

20:50.540 --> 20:54.110
<i>This monster slays even past defeats.</i>

20:54.400 --> 20:56.110
I'll ask again.

20:56.110 --> 20:59.210
Is there anything you'd like 
to say before you die?

21:00.440 --> 21:02.590
I've always contemplated it...

21:02.590 --> 21:07.160
What should I say in the short time I have 
before the flame of my life is extinguished?

21:08.200 --> 21:11.840
It was just now, just seconds ago,
that I finally knew.

21:11.840 --> 21:13.780
I need no words.

21:14.300 --> 21:16.330
I need only action!

21:17.460 --> 21:18.750
He's manipulating his shirt 
with his special ability?!

21:23.000 --> 21:24.430
A fire extinguisher from the ship!

21:35.490 --> 21:36.890
He got away.

21:50.660 --> 21:52.530
I need no words.

21:53.110 --> 21:55.150
I need only action!

21:56.310 --> 21:58.000
He's manipulating his shirt 
with his special ability?!

22:01.510 --> 22:03.290
A fire extinguisher from the ship!

22:10.790 --> 22:13.640
Action over words in this moment?

22:14.340 --> 22:16.370
Bravo!

22:20.900 --> 22:22.320
Akutagawa!
